rsort is a Rust reimplementation of macOS sort, whose source is BSD sort
from FreeBSD as shipped in Apple's text_cmds
(https://github.com/apple-oss-distributions/text_cmds, commit 592aaf8). No
C code is copied, but parts of rsort follow that source's logic closely so
that its output matches: string collation (bwscoll), number reading and
comparison (read_number, numcoll), version sort (vcmp), general numbers
(bwstod), locale setup, -t parsing, and the obsolete +POS key rewrite
(fix_obsolete_keys). That source carries this notice:

